@owner: mason
@stability: internal
@since: 2026-10-15
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: User Config Writer
  "Merges setup's results (server, key, share store) into ~/.mason, preserving the user's other keys and comments."

  Provides:
    - setup.WriteUserConfig @source("symbol:WriteUserConfig")
    - setup.UserConfigValues @source("symbol:UserConfigValues")
    - setup.UserConfigWrite @source("symbol:UserConfigWrite")

  Consumes:
    - config.Load

  Invariants:
    - Empty values MUST leave the corresponding key untouched
    - Existing comments and unrelated keys MUST survive the merge
    - A v1 file MUST be moved to <path>.v1.bak before a fresh v2 file is written, and the backup path reported
    - The merged result MUST load through config.Load before it replaces the file; an invalid result MUST leave the original untouched
    - An unchanged result MUST NOT rewrite the file

  OutOfScope:
    - Project .mason files (setup.InitProject)
    - Deciding which values to record (setup.Run)

  Scenario (happy-path): Fresh machine
    Given no ~/.mason
    When WriteUserConfig records server example.com and key ~/.ssh/mason
    Then ~/.mason contains exactly those two keys

  Scenario (happy-path): Add a share store to an existing file
    Given ~/.mason with a comment and server
    When WriteUserConfig records a share URL
    Then the comment and server remain and share is added

  Scenario (negative): v1 file present
    Given ~/.mason in the default/targets shape
    When WriteUserConfig runs
    Then the old file is kept as ~/.mason.v1.bak and a v2 file is written

  Scenario (edge): Nothing changed
    Given ~/.mason already records the same values
    When WriteUserConfig runs
    Then the file is not rewritten and Changed is false
